-- title:
--   Identification of branches with Igusa valuation rings
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. The field $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ carries the modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$, the subfield of $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$-Laurent series generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC`; $W$ is a finite set of places of this field over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ (a place being a proper valuation subring containing the base field whose ideals are principal), and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, namely the places that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and at which the value of `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`. Inside the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the hypothesis `hle` records the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into the base change of the function field of level $q^2M'$ with the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$, the kernel of the reduction map on unit groups attached to `dvd_sq_mul q M'`.
--
--   The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the residue-field modular function field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, the condition that $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ meets the constants in exactly $A$ and induces the residue map of $A$ there, the possibility of scaling any nonzero element by a constant into $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue, and compatibility of divisors with the map on places. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that $R_0$ is the coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the series obtained from $y$ by reducing each coefficient.
--
--   Further data: a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$; a family $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) $= \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$; and a family $O^{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa group of hypotheses. `hIg_inf` describes $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ at the standard point $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q = [1:0]$: an element $f$ lies in it precisely when there are Laurent series $x, y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is nonzero and $f$ times the image of $y$ equals the image of $x$. `hIg` says every $\ell$ is obtained from $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ by some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$: the reduction $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma$ carries $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ to $\ell$ and $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$. `hIg_inj` says the family is injective, and `hIg_perm` that for every primitive root $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ permutes the family, i.e. equals $O^{\mathrm{Ig}} \circ \sigma$ for some permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$.
--
--   The supersingular group of hypotheses. `hSS_A` says each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ lies over $A$: a constant lies in it iff it lies in $A$. `hSS_over` relates $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ to the place $s$ through $R_0$: for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the base-changed $q$-expansion $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,jq$ of $j$ has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix` says each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr` provides, for each $s \in W$, an element $t \in O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t$ minus the image of any $a \in A$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   The Igusa ring at $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ is further given as the ring of integers of a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, q^2M', \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ — a valuation subring with surjective residue map onto that field, kernel the maximal ideal, intersection $A$ with the constants, compatibility with the residue map of $A$, and the scaling property — via `hR` $: R.\mathrm{integers} = O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$; and `hR₀O` says that an element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if its image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   The arithmetic group of hypotheses on the base. There is $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$. There is an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that the contraction $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; and `hκ` says $k_0 \cap A$ meets every residue class: every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$. There is a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $A_1$ is the valuation subring of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (`hA₁`), assumed to be a discrete valuation ring and Henselian.
--
--   With $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the conclusion is a statement about every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ subject to four conditions: (i) the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is everything; (ii) $F_0$ is stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (iii) a linear disjointness condition: for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$, and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the vanishing of $\sum_i c_i a_i$ forces all $a_i = 0$; (iv) every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ whose underlying Laurent series lies in the image of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum inside $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$. Given an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is compatible with the inclusions, in the sense that the image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the image of $a \in A_1$ is the image of $a$ under $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; given $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is the inclusion of the element $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,jq$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, with $j_1 \ne 0$; given $\varpi \in A_1$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_1$; and given a valuation subring $V$ of $T_1$ such that the image of every element of $A_1$ lies in $V$, the image of $\varpi$ is a non-unit of $V$, and for every polynomial $P \in A_1[X]$ not divisible by the constant $\varpi$ both $P(j_1)$ and $P(j_1)^{-1}$ lie in $V$: then there exists a point of [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) — the conclusion reuses the letter $\ell$ for this bound variable — such that for every $f \in T_1$, $f$ lies in $V$ if and only if the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$.
--
--   Thus $V$ is exactly the contraction to $T_1$ of one of the Igusa valuation subrings of the full level field.
--
--   This is the branch-identification step in the analysis of the special fibre at $q$ of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with the subgroup `levelH q M'`: a valuation subring of the level field $T_1 = K_1 \cdot F_0$ that contains $A_1$, makes a uniformiser a non-unit, and makes every polynomial in $j_1$ prime to $\varpi$ a unit, is forced to be the trace of one of the $q+1$ Igusa rings, the valuation-theoretic form of Igusa's description of the components of the reduction. It feeds the later results on the two-chart integral model, on maximal ideals of the Drinfeld ring of the finite chart algebra, and on the rational places of that descent.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_forall_coe_mem_igusa_iff_of_valuationSubring_levelField.lean

